Third-party material in benchmarks/
===================================

tpu_verilog, tpu_spire
----------------------

Derived from LogikBench, https://github.com/zeroasiccorp/logikbench,
commit e8c7c4388c66302c6adb235678512ce62b79968a (e8c7c43), directory
logikbench/benchmarks/large/tpu/rtl/.

  Copyright (c) 2025 Zero ASIC Corporation
  Author (per the source file headers): Andreas Olofsson
  License: MIT. The upstream LICENSE file of that commit is reproduced
  verbatim as benchmarks/LICENSE.

What is taken from upstream and how:

  tpu_verilog/_debug/orig/tpu.v, tpu_array.v, tpu_pe.v
      Verbatim copies of the upstream RTL.
  tpu_verilog/context/starting_point.v
      tpu_pe.v + tpu_array.v + tpu.v concatenated, otherwise unmodified.
  tpu_spire/context/starting_point.py
      A Spire HDL port of the same design (register-for-register mirror),
      written for this suite.
  tpu_*/vectors.dat
      Stimulus generated by tpu_verilog/_debug/gen_stimuli.py, with the
      expected outputs recorded from the upstream RTL through
      tpu_verilog/_debug/tb_golden_dump.sv.

The testbench (tb.sv), the stimulus generator, the task descriptions and the
metadata files were written for this suite and are covered by the LICENSE at
the root of this repository.

jpeg_idct_2d_verilog
--------------------

Derived from core_jpeg, https://github.com/ultraembedded/core_jpeg (main
branch, 2026-07), files src_v/jpeg_idct_x.v, jpeg_idct_transpose.v,
jpeg_idct_transpose_ram.v, jpeg_idct_y.v.

  Copyright 2020 Ultra-Embedded.com (per the source file headers)
  License: Apache License 2.0, reproduced verbatim as benchmarks/LICENSE-apache-2.0.

What is taken from upstream and how:

  jpeg_idct_2d_verilog/context/starting_point.v
      The four upstream modules, unmodified, under a thin top module
      (jpeg_idct_2d) that composes them exactly as the original jpeg_idct.v
      instantiates them (downstream ready tied high).
  jpeg_idct_2d_verilog/vectors.dat
      Stimulus generated by _debug/gen_vectors.py, with the expected outputs
      recorded from the upstream RTL (recipe in _debug/README.md).

The testbench (tb.sv), the stimulus generator, the task description and the
metadata file were written for this suite and are covered by the LICENSE at
the root of this repository.

pdpu_dot16_pipe_verilog
-----------------------

Derived from PDPU, https://github.com/qleenju/PDPU (ISCAS 2023), main branch
as of 2026-08-04, module pdpu_top_pipelined and the modules it instantiates.

  License: Apache License 2.0, reproduced verbatim as benchmarks/LICENSE-apache-2.0.
  Two helper modules inside the upstream sources carry headers of ETH Zurich
  and the University of Bologna under the Solderpad Hardware License 0.51;
  those headers are kept in place in context/starting_point.v.

What is taken from upstream and how:

  pdpu_dot16_pipe_verilog/context/starting_point.v
      The upstream SystemVerilog with N raised from 4 to 16 and the rewrites
      yosys's front end needs (listed in the file header): hierarchy,
      arithmetic and pipeline cut points verbatim.
  pdpu_dot16_pipe_verilog/tb.sv
      Embeds the upstream combinational unit as the golden reference model.

The streaming testbench, the stimulus generator, the task description and the
metadata file were written for this suite and are covered by the LICENSE at
the root of this repository.

fpmul_f16_verilog
-----------------

Testbench and golden reference from the fpmul_f16 benchmark of RTL Scout,
https://github.com/huawei-csl/rtlscout (BSD-3-Clause-Clear, reproduced
verbatim as benchmarks/LICENSE-rtlscout).

What is taken from there and how:

  fpmul_f16_verilog/tb.sv
      Unmodified: it embeds the reference multiplier and enumerates the
      operand pairs itself.
  fpmul_f16_verilog/golden/design.v
      The reference multiplier (Spire HDL source compiled to Verilog),
      unmodified; used by the equivalence check, not shown to the agent.

context/starting_point.v, the task description and the metadata file were
written for this suite and are covered by the LICENSE at the root of this
repository.

cv32e40p_alu_verilog
--------------------

Derived from the CV32E40P RISC-V core of the OpenHW Group,
https://github.com/openhwgroup/cv32e40p, commit
6033d2b1be3295ec774d17ac4cf226faacfdeb08 (6033d2b), files rtl/cv32e40p_alu.sv,
rtl/cv32e40p_popcnt.sv, rtl/cv32e40p_ff_one.sv, rtl/cv32e40p_alu_div.sv and
rtl/include/cv32e40p_pkg.sv.

  Copyright 2018 ETH Zurich and University of Bologna
  License: Solderpad Hardware License, Version 0.51, reproduced verbatim as
  benchmarks/LICENSE-solderpad-0.51. The upstream file headers are kept in
  place in context/starting_point.sv and in the reference copy inside tb.sv.

What is taken from upstream and how:

  cv32e40p_alu_verilog/_debug/orig/*.sv
      Verbatim copies of the five upstream files.
  cv32e40p_alu_verilog/context/starting_point.sv
      The four RTL modules concatenated into one file by _debug/make_flattened.py:
      the package import is removed, the opcode and vector-mode constants are
      inlined as localparams and the enum-typed operator port is declared
      logic [6:0]. No logic is changed.
  cv32e40p_alu_verilog/tb.sv
      Embeds the same flattened upstream ALU as the reference model, with every
      module renamed (suffix __ref).
  cv32e40p_alu_verilog/vectors.dat
      Stimulus generated by _debug/gen_stimuli.py and _debug/gen_divheavy_vectors.py,
      with the expected outputs recorded from the upstream RTL through
      _debug/gen_tb.sv and cross-checked by _debug/sanity_check.py.

The testbench, the stimulus generators, the task description and the metadata
file were written for this suite and are covered by the LICENSE at the root of
this repository.
